/*
 * Shared test fixture — not shipped in any package.
 *
 * A real Frontier journal `Loadout` event for the same Federal Corvette (`ShipID` 44) as the
 * rail-gun refit, in an earlier fit (48 `Modules`): two huge plasma accelerators, a large
 * gimballed burst laser, a Rocket Propelled FSD Disruptor, a medium fragment cannon, a
 * Cytoscrambler burst laser, a small rail gun, eight shield boosters and four hull reinforcements.
 *
 * Contributed 2026-08-09 UTC by the repository owner from their own fleet, with no upstream
 * project. Stored SHA-256 `810748968e0cca8b8b209f90b1927668c1b0ede492478b720d2b5f5ddd234b99`. It
 * reached this repository as pasted text and is stored re-indented and otherwise unaltered, so the
 * checksum attests to the stored file rather than to a file Frontier wrote.
 *
 * Its grade-4 fragment cannon under `Weapon_Overcharged` folds no clip leg, the second of the
 * three weapon groups that says the penalty stops at the multi-cannon. It is also the only reading
 * of a fragment cannon's and a Rocket Propelled FSD Disruptor's own `DamagePerSecond`.
 *
 * `ShipName`, `ShipIdent`, `ShipID` and `timestamp` are kept — they describe a ship, and nothing
 * in the event names a person. The engineer names are the game's own NPCs.
 *
 * The capture is Elite Dangerous game output and remains the property of Frontier Developments
 * plc, redistributed under Frontier's media-usage terms; see ATTRIBUTIONS.md.
 */
